{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"18f0d2e7687b196dac119574c3a9cc422f7bf67adef478c326b34e326e203c6c","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review batch runner","key_entities":["ProductionBatchRunner.run","_project_criteria","orchestrator.route_criteria","workflow_ops.py:254-263","production_batch_runner.py:112","production_batch_runner.py:257","BatchRunRequest.with_inputs","gates/plan-review.yaml:60-62","probe_criteria","E4","G1G2"],"problem_keywords":["probe allowlist","project criteria routing","drift-refresh","probe mode filtering","batch step","plan review"],"propositions":["Project criteria activated via _project_criteria are evaluated during probe mode without filtering through the probe allowlist, causing extra billable LLM calls beyond the intended cheap probe set.","The probe allowlist (probe_criteria) is available as gate input but is not threaded to the batch step's with_inputs, preventing project criteria suppression.","Probe allowlist filtering should mirror workflow_ops semantics: retain only criteria ids present in the allowlist, suppressing project.* ids outside E4/G1G2 during probe mode.","The _project_criteria helper must accept a third parameter (probe id collection) and filter returned project criteria against it when non-empty."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787674737118046001,"uuid":"209b5f76-f578-4532-b19b-478deb46e82f"}